Law texts

The texts in this repository are the Constitution of the State of Sabah and Sabah Ordinances and Enactments as
published, in English, on Sabah Lawnet (https://sagc.sabah.gov.my) by the State Attorney-General's Chambers, Sabah.
Each PDF is stamped "FOR REFERENCE ONLY (<month> <year>)".

- Copyright: the Copyright Act 1987 [Act 332] of Malaysia, section 3, defines "literary work" and ends: "but does not
  include official texts of the Government or statutory bodies of a legislative or regulatory nature, or judicial
  decisions, or political speeches and political debates, or speeches delivered in the course of legal proceedings,
  and the official translation thereof". (Quoted from the Attorney General's Chambers' online reprint of Act 332, as
  at 1 July 2012.) The Constitution, Ordinances and Enactments are official texts of a legislative nature.
- The site's footer reads "Copyright (c) The State Attorney-General's Chambers." Its "Terms & Conditions" and
  "Disclaimer" links lead to the home page; the site states no terms that restrict reuse.
- The texts are reproduced without change to their wording; only the arrangement (one file per Article or section,
  one paragraph per line) is Lexifina's. The State Attorney-General's Chambers does not endorse this repository.

Attribution: Source: State Attorney-General's Chambers, Sabah, Sabah Lawnet, https://sagc.sabah.gov.my.

